@format 1
@id ui-event.e8cf2c58d99f679b
@title Roster Schedule — schedule item change
@section I. UI
@area UI event
@tabs Worklist
@event-ref cs|PMainArea/PRoster.cs|PRoster|pRosterSchedule|LScheduleItemChange|1
@entry input
@summary Handle the schedule item change event emitted by Roster Schedule through the exact route registered in PRoster.PRoster.
@tag schedule item change
@tag PRoster
@alias owner = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PRoster
@alias courier = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LCourier
@alias tabset = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.LTabset

[input] UI event <input>
- Receive the schedule item change event from Roster Schedule through its current registration @ owner.PRoster
> route

[route] Registered handler path <process>
- Refresh the changed work row @ owner.PRosterItemHandle
> detail-check

[detail-check] Should selected detail refresh? <decision>
- Compare the notice kind and changed item with the selected work @ owner.PRosterItemHandle
? "Progress notice or another item is selected" > output
? "Selected item has a non-progress change" > detail

[detail] Refresh selected-work detail <process>
- Resolve the displayed title from a live tab, cached stable stage, saved-plan source stage, or recorded work-tab fallback @ courier.LCourierWorkTitleRead(...)
@ tabset.LTabsetTitleRead(...)
- Rebuild the selected-work detail @ owner.PRosterItemHandle
> output

[output] UI state after the event <output>
= The changed row is current, and selected non-progress changes also refresh detail with the durable stage title when available.
